{{!
    @template theme_tresa/frontpage-steps
    Front page "How it works" - a static 3-step process explainer, each
    step fading in a little after the last as the section scrolls into
    view (see lib.php: theme_tresa_get_frontpage_steps_context()).

    Context: steps.title, steps.steps [{number, icon, title, text, delay}].

    Note the dot-notation throughout, on both the interpolation tags and
    the section tags around the loop below: this partial is included
    directly into theme_tresa/frontpage as a plain partial reference, not
    wrapped in a section of its own, so it shares that template's WHOLE
    top-level context rather than getting one scoped to just this section's
    own data - same reason theme_tresa/course-grid already references
    "coursegrid.title"/"coursegrid.courses" instead of bare "title"/
    "courses". Using the bare, undotted section name here previously meant
    it resolved to the wrapper hash itself (title + the list, together) - a
    single hash, not a list, so Mustache pushed it as one context rather
    than looping - instead of the list of 3 step items one level inside it.

    IMPORTANT: never write the two-character closing-brace sequence inside
    this comment block, not even as a quoted example describing this exact
    rule - Mustache's own comment parser isn't brace-depth aware, so it
    ends the comment at the very first occurrence of that sequence,
    wherever it appears, illustrative or not. Getting this wrong twice
    already (once with a literal example tag, once with that same sequence
    quoted while describing the rule) silently leaked the rest of this
    comment's own text as visible page content, without even raising an
    error the second time - worth being paranoid about re-reading this
    whole block for that sequence before ever touching it again.
}}
<section class="tresa-steps tresa-section tresa-section--alt">
    <div class="tresa-steps__header">
        <h2 class="tresa-steps__title">{{steps.title}}</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tresa-steps__grid">
        {{#steps.steps}}
        <div class="tresa-step tresa-reveal" style="transition-delay: {{delay}}ms;">
            <span class="tresa-step__number">{{number}}</span>
            <span class="tresa-step__icon"><i class="fa {{icon}}" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
            <h3 class="tresa-step__title">{{title}}</h3>
            <p class="tresa-step__text">{{text}}</p>
        </div>
        {{/steps.steps}}
    </div>
</section>
